summary: 'Wondering why your 5GB bundle finished in just 2 days? Here are 5 practical smartphone settings you can change right now to save your mobile data on MTN and Telecel.'
---

Almost every smartphone user in Ghana has experienced this before. You load a fresh data bundle on your phone, you barely opened YouTube, but within 48 hours, your balance is already sitting at zero.

The truth is that modern smartphones are designed to consume high-speed internet in the background without asking you first. High-resolution video feeds, automatic cloud backups, and social media autoplay eat up gigabytes quietly while your phone is sitting in your pocket.

Here are 5 simple, effective settings you can adjust right now on Android and iPhone to make your data last twice as long.

## 1. Turn off WhatsApp auto-download on mobile data

WhatsApp is often the biggest hidden data drain in Ghana. Every day, people send large videos, voice notes, and memes into family and work groups. If your WhatsApp is set to download media automatically, your phone downloads every single file using your mobile data.

**How to fix it:**
- Open WhatsApp.
- Go to **Settings > Storage and Data**.
- Under **Media auto-download**, tap on **When using mobile data**.
- Uncheck **Photos, Audio, Videos, and Documents**.
- Now you can choose to only download files you actually want to see.

## 2. Set TikTok and Instagram to Data Saver Mode

Short-form video apps stream in high definition by default. Scrolling TikTok or Instagram Reels for just 30 minutes can easily burn through 400MB to 700MB of data.

**On TikTok:**
- Go to your Profile > Settings & Privacy.
- Scroll down to **Data Saver** and switch it ON.

**On Instagram:**
- Go to Settings > Account > Cellular Data Use.
- Turn on **Data Saver** and select High Resolution Media over **Wi-Fi Only**.

## 3. Restrict background data usage for heavy apps

Many apps keep refreshing their content, downloading new ads, and updating feeds in the background even when you have closed them.

**On Android:**
- Open **Settings > Apps**.
- Select apps like Facebook, Twitter (X), or Chrome.
- Tap **Mobile data & Wi-Fi** and turn off **Background data**.

**On iPhone:**
- Open **Settings > General > Background App Refresh**.
- Turn it off completely or choose Wi-Fi only.

## 4. Turn off automatic cloud backups over cellular data

Google Photos and Apple iCloud often back up your camera roll automatically. If you take 20 photos or record a short video at an event, your phone will quietly upload gigabytes of media using your paid data bundle.

Go into your Google Photos or iCloud settings and make sure **Back up over mobile data** is strictly disabled.

## 5. Buy bigger bundles with better per-gigabyte pricing

Buying 1GB five separate times across a week always costs you significantly more money than buying a single 5GB or 10GB bundle upfront. 

Bulk packages come with cheaper rates per gigabyte and longer validity windows, saving you money in the long run.

